I'll start by orienting on the project and the design contract.The atlas indexed the platform root, so I'll work with the `codx-junior-ui` child project paths directly.Now I have what I need. Embedding `WikiView` (already mobile-aware: off-canvas drawer + hamburger at <480px) is the low-risk path, so `WikiView.vue` stays untouched and `/wiki` keeps working.The dev client container is running — let me verify the SFC there.Container exec rejects multi-statement commands, so I'll write a small scratch checker (same pattern as the existing `tmp/sfc-check.cjs`) and run it.Found a real blocker by tracing `WikiView.syncUrl()`: it rebuilds the query string from scratch, so any page click inside the embedded wiki **drops `?tab=library`** and `ChannelView.activeTab` would fall back to Home, unmounting the wiki. Small targeted fix:**Library tab now renders the real documentation.**

What I did (reuse over rewrite — the extraction into `WikiBrowser.vue` was rejected as too risky for a 1 280-line view, the step explicitly allows embedding):

1. `ChannelView.vue`
   - `import WikiView from '@/views/WikiView.vue'` in `<script setup>` + `components: { WikiView }` (project convention), so the Library tab renders the *same* documentation browser served by `/:projectName/wiki` — page tree, search, "on this page" rail and assistant included.
   - Panel wrapper no longer scrolls for that tab (`overflow-hidden` vs `overflow-y-auto`) so the wiki owns its own scroll containers instead of nesting them; Library section is `h-full min-h-0`.
   - Library tab meta dropped its placeholder/`link` fields and the now-unreachable placeholder `RouterLink`; `/wiki` stays reachable through a compact header icon (`:to="{ name: 'wiki' }"`) shown only on the Library tab.
   - Narrow screens: `WikiView` already collapses its tree into an off-canvas drawer behind a "Docs" button below 480 px, so the article is readable at 360 px with no horizontal overflow (wrapper is `overflow-hidden`, article padding `px-5`, `pre`/tables keep their own `overflow-x`).

2. `WikiView.vue` — one 8-line fix that was *required* for embedding: `syncUrl()` rebuilt the query string from an empty `URLSearchParams`, so the first page click inside the embedded wiki dropped `?tab=library`, `activeTab` fell back to `home` and the wiki unmounted. It now starts from the existing params, preserving unrelated ones and still normalising `project`/`page` (behaviour on `/wiki` is unchanged — there are no other params there).

